### Try the API from VS Code with the REST Client extension (click "Send Request").
@api = http://localhost:8000/api

### Health
GET {{api}}/health

### Route between two towns
GET {{api}}/network/route?from=Lusaka&to=Kasama

### Public: submit a quote request
POST {{api}}/quotes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test Customer",
  "phone": "+260 97 000 0000",
  "pickup": "Lusaka",
  "delivery": "Kitwe",
  "cargo": "Chilled or frozen food",
  "weight": 5,
  "service": "One-off load"
}

### Public: track a load
GET {{api}}/tracking/ELL-7K3Q9

### Staff: sign in (create a user first with `make user`)
# @name login
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "you@example.com", "password": "your-password" }

### Staff: list quotes
GET {{api}}/quotes
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Staff: list active loads
GET {{api}}/loads?stage=active
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Leave a review (public; waits for approval)
POST {{api}}/reviews
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Grace Phiri", "company": "Phiri General Dealers", "town": "Chipata", "rating": 5, "comment": "Arrived on time and in good condition.", "contact": "+260 95 000 0404" }

### Approved reviews (public)
GET {{api}}/reviews

### All reviews for moderation (staff)
GET {{api}}/reviews/all?status=pending
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Approve a review (staff)
PATCH {{api}}/reviews/1
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "approved" }
